1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:04,000
AI agents can already move money and use powerful tools.

2
00:00:04,100 --> 00:00:07,400
But being able to do something doesn't mean they're allowed to do it.

3
00:00:07,500 --> 00:00:10,700
This is Auctorail.

4
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:14,400
Here, invoice-bot may pay one specific vendor,

5
00:00:14,500 --> 00:00:17,600
up to five USDC per transaction.

6
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:21,900
Now it requests a one USDC supplier invoice.

7
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:26,300
Auctorail freezes the exact request and checks the permission.

8
00:00:26,600 --> 00:00:29,800
It verifies delegated authority, then asks Telegraph

9
00:00:29,900 --> 00:00:33,000
for fraud intelligence on this exact recipient.

10
00:00:33,300 --> 00:00:36,100
The evidence matches the wallet and the Base Sepolia network,

11
00:00:36,200 --> 00:00:38,800
and the requested action.

12
00:00:39,100 --> 00:00:42,000
Every check passes and one-use authority is issued.

13
00:00:42,100 --> 00:00:46,300
A real Base Sepolia transaction is confirmed on-chain.

14
00:00:46,600 --> 00:00:50,000
Now the agent tries to send more than was approved.

15
00:00:50,100 --> 00:00:52,600
The old authorization no longer matches. Blocked.

16
00:00:52,700 --> 00:00:55,300
No transaction is sent.

17
00:00:55,600 --> 00:00:59,300
And if required evidence isn't available, Auctorail doesn't guess.

18
00:00:59,400 --> 00:01:03,000
It holds the action instead of spending.

19
00:01:03,300 --> 00:01:06,100
Intelligence tells agents what they know.

20
00:01:06,200 --> 00:01:09,000
Auctorail determines what they're allowed to do.

